    "share_count_basis": "1,558.05M common shares outstanding at 2026-07-31 (10-Q cover, dei:EntityCommonStockSharesOutstanding); Q2-26 weighted diluted 1,555M, dilutive securities immaterial (~1M options, ~9M unvested RSUs largely in the treasury-method count). Includes the 6.6M shares issued for BTIG on 2026-06-01. Held FLAT: SBC is charged in the flows and buybacks are a use of the FCFE already being valued.",
    "wacc_rationale": "The discount rate is a COST OF EQUITY, not a WACC: the flow is post-interest, post-preferred FCFE. US 10y ~4.2% + beta ~1.05 x 5.5% ERP = ~10.0%. Base 10.0% (USB is a higher-quality, lower-loss-history franchise than TFC at 10.5%); bull 9.75%; bear 10.5% (credit path already carries most of the bear, so only +50bp to avoid charging risk twice).",
    "lease_treatment": "n/a -- bank; occupancy cost is inside noninterest expense, no lease charge modelled separately.",
    "nci_treatment": "NCI ($463M equity, ~$24M/yr income) and preferred dividends (~$371M/yr TTM incl. participating-securities allocation) are removed INSIDE the flow: the 'EBITDA' line is pre-tax income less a pre-tax-equivalent of pref dividends + NCI income, so the after-tax flow is net income to COMMON. Preferred is therefore NOT also deducted in the equity bridge (doing both would charge it twice).",
    "notes": "MODEL: bank -> FCFE at cost of equity through the component engine (house precedent TFC, HBAN, NTRS, STT, NAB.AX; SKILL.md routes banks to residual income on tangible book -- FCFE-at-CoE with retention = growth x regulatory capital is the equivalent flow form and keeps USB comparable with the other US banks in this folder). Engine mapping: revenue = net interest income + noninterest income (GAAP, $29,583M TTM; the XBRL 'Revenues' tag / CSV Revenue column is $29,694M, ~0.4% higher, and is not used); 'ebitda' = pre-tax income + SBC - pre-tax-equivalent(pref dividends + NCI income) = $9,958M = 33.66% of revenue TTM; D&A 0; 'capex' = capital retention required to grow CET1 with the balance sheet = revenue x CET1/revenue (1.646) x g/(1+g); wc 0; net_debt 0 (deposits and wholesale debt are operating funding). TTM build: pre-tax 10,204 = revenue 29,583 - noninterest expense 17,117 - provision 2,262; tax 2,012 (19.7%); NI 8,168; NI to common 7,797. CET1 capital ~$48.7B = 10.8% x RWA ~$451B (RWA backed out of TCE/RWA 9.4%); TCE $42.4B (equity 67,432 - preferred 6,808 - goodwill 13,234 - other intangibles 4,999), AOCI -$7,111M. last_fcf 5,470 = NI to common 7,797 less retention to grow CET1 at the TTM loan-growth-adjusted 5% (~$2.3B): an FCFE proxy, since bank OCF is meaningless. Equity bridge: BTIG contingent cash consideration (up to $275M over 3 years). Excess CET1: none credited -- CET1 is 10.8% at both Dec-25 and Jun-26, management runs it flat, and the March 2026 capital proposals are 'expected to be favorable' but unquantified. Upside not in the model: AOCI pull-to-par and any capital relief from the 2026 rule proposals.",
